  (text "TX AUDIO SELECT - relay switches what reaches the aircraft's mic\njack between ADAU1861's own analog output (AeroNode speaking) and\nthe pilot's boom mic (from the earcup), per Peter 2026-09-29.\n\nK1 = G6K-2F-Y (same qualified relay used on the H1 headset-mute\nboard - bifurcated crossbar contacts, rated for dry-circuit audio,\nNOT a generic silver-contact relay). Only pole A is used; pole B\n(pins 21/22/24) is unused and marked no-connect.\n\nFAIL-PASSIVE CHOICE (mine, not yet confirmed by Peter): de-energized\n(NC, pin 12) = BOOM_MIC_FROM_EARCUP - the pilot's own mic still\nreaches the aircraft if power/control is lost. Energized (NO, pin\n14) = HPOUTP - AeroNode's audio reaches the aircraft mic input only\nwhen actively driven. Confirm this is the wanted default before fab.\n\nQ1/D1/R10 = standard low-side coil driver: GPIO_RLY_TX_SEL_3V3 (a\nnew signal on J1 pin 4, previously spare) -> 2N7002 gate, R10 100k\ngate pulldown for fail-passive (relay stays de-energized if the GPIO\nis high-Z during host boot), D1 flyback diode across the coil.\n\nRELAY COIL SUPPLY - RESOLVED per Peter 2026-09-29, option 1 of 4\nconsidered (see chat: dedicated regulator / PWM coil economiser /\ndifferent relay / borrow a 5V rail from aeronode). Fetched Omron's\nown G6K datasheet (not cached anywhere in this repo before now):\nmust-operate <=80% of rated, must-release >=10%, max voltage 150%\nof rated is EXPLICITLY INSTANTANEOUS ONLY, not continuous. Checked\nevery stock coil option (3/4.5/5/12/24 VDC) against VBAT 5.0-7.3V -\nnone spans it cleanly. The 5V coil is the only contender, but\nVBAT_max (7.3V = 146% of rated) held continuously is right at the\nedge of a rating the datasheet says not to run continuously.\n\nFIX: U11 (ADP7118AUJZ-1.8-R7 - the SAME part already used twice on\nthis board as U9/U10, just wired in its ADJUSTABLE configuration\ninstead of the fixed pass-through) regulates VBAT down to a fixed\n4.5V RLY_COIL_SUPPLY rail, independent of VBAT's swing entirely.\n4.5V sits above the 5V coil's 4.0V guaranteed-operate floor (80%)\nwith margin, and 0.5V below VBAT_min (5.0V) gives an LDO at 21mA\ncomfortable dropout headroom (datasheet: 200mV @ 200mA - trivial\nat this load). R11 (15k)/R12 (10k) set VOUT = 1.8V*(1+R1/R2) = 4.5V,\nper the ADP7118 datasheet's own adjustable-mode formula (Fig. 39),\nR2 well under its 200k max-recommended value. EN tied to VIN for\nauto-start, 2.2uF on VIN and VOUT per datasheet minimum - same\npattern as U9/U10's power note on the main sheet.\n\nOPEN ITEMS - not resolved by this pass:\n1. HPOUTP is tapped RAW off U1 (no series R/C, no clamp). The H1\n   board's equivalent injection used a 220nF+10k blocking network\n   plus a BAT54S clamp because the far end carries aircraft mic\n   bias (8-16V) that could exceed the ADAU1861's 2.1V abs-max input\n   ceiling. That protection is NOT yet replicated here - do this\n   before connecting to a real aircraft mic circuit.\n2. J5 (3.5mm TRS -> PJ068 adapter) Ring is left NO-CONNECT - bias\n   pass-through from the aircraft to the boom mic capsule is\n   undesigned. Sleeve ties straight to this board's AGND, i.e. NO\n   isolation from aircraft ground (unlike the transformer-isolated\n   H1 board) - flagged, not designed out.\n3. J4 (boom mic from earcup) and J5 are generic placeholders, same\n   convention as J1/J2/J3 on the main sheet - real connectors once\n   the mechanical interface is chosen.\n4. Second transistor/relay pole, footprint for K1 (G6K package is\n   1-8, not the generic Relay_DPDT symbol's EN50005 numbering) -\n   same open item as the H1 board's K1/K2, not resolved here either.\n5. U11's aggregate load on VBAT is trivial (21mA) and doesn't touch\n   the U10/3V3_ACCEL budget flagged in the power note - a genuinely\n   separate rail, deliberately, so the relay coil can never brown\n   out the accelerometer/translator stack or vice versa."
    (at 240 180 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
    (uuid "c70de790-0870-495a-9d8a-4c63101c048a")
  )
